course: dictionary
lesson: 3596
title: One word, many meanings: fierce
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have several meanings, and fierce is a good example. It can mean angry and ready to attack, very strong, or full of strong feeling. The words around it tell you which meaning to use.
explain: «A fierce dog» means a dog that is angry and likely to attack. «A fierce storm» means a storm that is very strong. Look at the word that comes after fierce: it is often the clue.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «fierce competition», the word competition is about strong effort, not an angry animal. Slang is different again: if someone says «You look fierce!», they mean you look bold and confident, so think about who is speaking and where.
fact: Fierce means angry, wild and likely to attack, as in «a fierce dog».
fact: Fierce also means very strong or powerful, as in «a fierce storm» and «fierce heat».
fact: Fierce can mean full of strong feeling or effort, as in «fierce competition» and «fierce rivals».
fact: In slang, «You look fierce!» means someone looks bold and confident in a cool way.
fact: The forms are fierce, fiercer and fiercest: you add -er to compare two things and -est to compare three or more.
exercise: «The fierce dog barked at the postman.» What does fierce mean here? | Very quiet | Lost in the park | *Angry and likely to attack | Friendly and sleepy
exercise: «A fierce storm blew the roof off the barn.» What does fierce mean? | Calm and still | Gentle and warm | *Very strong and powerful | Full of colour
exercise: Maya says, «You look fierce in that jacket!» What does she mean? | Lost in the rain | *Bold and confident in a cool way | Angry with her friend | Hot and sweaty
test: «The two fierce rivals raced for the lead in the last lap.» What does fierce mean here? | Wet and cold | Sleepy and slow | Dark and quiet | *Full of strong feeling and effort
test: Which sentence uses fierce to mean very strong? | *A fierce storm knocked down the fence. | We ate toast for breakfast. | The kitten had a soft, fluffy tail. | The bus was yellow.
exam: In «a fierce dog» and «a fierce storm», why do the words after fierce matter? | They can always be skipped | They mean the same thing as fierce | They are spelled wrongly and should be changed | *They are clues that show which meaning of fierce to use
